    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0295" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.9318/5.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 40.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 21, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 15th instant, in which you are good enough to inform
                    me that the Costa Rican Government has consented to the exercise of good offices
                    by American diplomatic and consular representatives in behalf of Chinese
                    lawfully resident in that country.</p>
                <pb facs="0296" n="180" xml:id="pg180"/>
                <p>I beg to express to you the sincere thanks of my Government for this act of true
                    friendship shown by the American Government toward China, which, I need hardly
                    assure you, is gratefully appreciated by the Chinese residents in Costa Rica as
                    well as by myself.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kai Fu Shah</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
